{"study_accession":"PRJEB106558","secondary_study_accession":"ERP187609","title":"A comparison of long read single cell transcriptomic approaches","description":"This project benchmarks long-read single-cell RNA sequencing technologies using matched cDNA generated with the 10x Genomics platform. We performed parallel sequencing of the same single-cell cDNA libraries on PacBio and Oxford Nanopore platforms, alongside standard Illumina short-read sequencing as a reference for data quality and transcript recovery. In addition, we evaluated the impact of CRISPR-based depletion of abundant transcripts prior to long-read sequencing to assess whether targeted removal improves transcriptome coverage and isoform representation. By analysing single-source cDNA across platforms, we provide a controlled comparison of long-read performance, examining read- and gene-level metrics, isoform detection, and concordance in clustering and cell type identification relative to the short-read standard. This work establishes a practical benchmarking framework for the optimisation and interpretation of long-read single-cell transcriptomic data","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":2,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMEA120422630","study_accession":"PRJEB106558","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"68f9ea91cfb0e7396a995a53:sample:pbmc2-illumina","description":"68f9ea91cfb0e7396a995a53:sample:pbmc2-illumina","sex":"","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":2,"first_public":"2026-01-16","attributes":[["ENA-CHECKLIST","ERC000011"],["Organism","Homo sapiens"],["organism","Homo sapiens"],["Sample","pbmc2-illumina"],["collection date","2022-12-13"],["scientific_name","Homo sapiens"],["common name","human"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["geographic location (country and/or sea)","United Kingdom"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"ERR16108678","experiment_accession":"ERX15498331","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSe